   "text": {
    "L1": "Rani Abbakka ruled Ullal, a port town on the Karnataka coast, in the 1500s.",
    "L2": "She refused to pay tax to the Portuguese and fought them for many years.",
    "L3": "Her courage and love of freedom guided her. She also showed leadership and unity.",
    "L4": "She joined hands with nearby rulers, bringing people together to defend their land.",
    "L5": "Here is a grammar rule: use she for Rani Abbakka, not he.",
    "L6": "Use who for a person, and which for a thing.",
    "L7": "So we say, “Rani Abbakka was a queen who fought the Portuguese.”",
    "L8": "For a thing, we say, “Rani Abbakka had a navy which attacked Portuguese ships.”"
   },
